# Security

See `docs/06-security/SECURITY_BASELINE.md`, `PERMISSION_MODEL.md`, and `AUDIT_TRAIL.md`.

- **Deny by default.** Every protected action passes Policies/Gates using `module.action` permissions. No authorization → no merge. No persona bypasses authorization — including the Tenant Owner.
- Authentication via Sanctum with rate limiting on auth endpoints; login success and security-relevant failures are audited.
- All input via Form Requests; mass-assignment protection on all models; all output via API Resources (no leakage of hashes, tokens, internal flags).
- **Never expose secrets**; no credentials in the repository; **never use production data locally**; no production credentials exist at this stage.
- **Audit every critical action** (user/role/permission changes, contract transitions, meeting completion, decision approval/closure, task assignment/completion, document upload/delete/sensitive download, inventory transactions, custody assign/return, tenant settings, logins). Passwords, tokens, and secrets never appear in audit values. Audit logs are immutable for normal users.
- Files: private storage only, authorized downloads, MIME/extension validation, size limits, tenant-isolated paths.
- Secure errors (standardized envelope, no stack traces in production); database constraints back up application rules; soft deletion where appropriate.
- Cross-tenant access attempts return `404` (see `03-multi-tenancy.mdc`).
- No formal compliance certification is claimed; Saudi PDPL and contractual requirements must be considered during implementation and deployment.
- Security-relevant changes require review by the other developer — no self-merge.
